{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas","id":593798,"title":"Variations on Renown and Harmony - critique and ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-17T08:07:52-07:00","id":593798,"title":"Variations on Renown and Harmony - critique and ideas?","content":"A bit of background: Our WoD chronicle is centered on a pack of Changing Breeds. We were drawing heavily from WtA, and I'm deliberately casting the Changing Breeds in this incarnation of the story as being the remnants of wars among those Luna had called to be equals. (Think, War of Rage, etc)<br /> <br /> For all of that, we've adopted the way the Garou / Uratha handle many of the shapeshifter systems - it's just much better supported and developed. All of our Fera are eligible for Gifts, and so on.<br /> <br /> Some of the things that we've been trying to improve on for our particular chronicle are Renown and Harmony.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The translations among Renowns and Respects was confusing, so we simplified down to just one stat, Renown. Renown measures how far and wide your reputation has spread. That counts for chatter among Spirits, among the People, and so on. It also counts for gaining Gifts, and so on.<br /> <br /> Because people who are renowned are renowned for doing things, we borrowed the idea of a specialization from the rules for skills. All of the previously existing Renowns and Respects are available as specializations, and there is always the possibility of more. Many of them overlap, but that's alright because we're used to that from dealing with skills.<br /> <br /> As an aside at this point, if Changing Breeds ever gets an update to Second Edition levels, I would implore the authors to use common terms between CB and WtF in all possible cases!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For Harmony, we weren't entirely satisfied by either implementation so far: the higher-is-better from WtF1 or the balanced extremities of WtF2. Both seemed to be missing something. What we came up with was to split Harmony in two: Harmony of Spirit and Harmony of Flesh. <br /> <br /> Each is on a scale of 1 to 5. We're operating on the idea that you lose something if one drops to 1 dot, and lose a lot if one drops to zero; and that you gain something if one goes to four dots and gain again if one goes to five dots. One or zero dots shuts down your ability to do certain shapeshifter things. Four dots grants a specialization of sorts for shapeshifting or Umbral or Spirit activities. Five dots grants a second specialization.<br /> <br /> For all rolls requiring a total Harmony, the two are added together. We're still using First-Edition rules as our basis for the time being, so Rites and Rituals for example would be a combined Harmony roll. <br /> <br /> Harmony of Spirit aids in entering the Umbra and in shapeshifting toward the spirit-animal side of the shapeshifting spectrum. Possible specializations would be bonuses toward controlling Kuruth, stepping sideways into the Umbra, cross-Gauntlet perception into the Umbra, or making Partial Change or a shapechange toward the spirit-animal side Reflexive.<br /> <br /> Harmony of Flesh aids in exiting the Umbra and in shapeshifting toward the human side of the spectrum. Possible specializations would be bonuses toward extending Kuruth, stepping sideways out of the Umbra, cross-Gauntlet perception out of the Umbra, or making a Partial Change or shapechange toward the human side Reflexive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is all in an early test with my group. <br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Obvious holes? Other possibilities that are opened up? Lots of ideas for specializations?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:21:25-07:00","id":594048,"title":"","content":"I doubt that they will use common terms among CB and Forsaken. Or that would be good. Even tough I agree the Fera approach is interesting, the Changing Breeds was designed to a broader approach, and it would be lost with too much of Werewolf rules in it.<br /> <br /> But your take on Harmony is interesting. Can't say I didn't liked 2nd ed Harmony, tough it could have a better Breaking Points list, but your taking is also a valid and fascinating one.<br /> <br /> What I don't agree is about Renown. Its a balance issue. You see, you're talking about the core supernatural set of attributes of the game. In every line, you have a Power Trait and a Supernatural Set of Attributes, lets call it SSA. Vampires have Disciplines, Mages have Arcana, Changelings have Contracts, and so on.<br /> <br /> The SSA have a clear function on the game, the same function for all of them, indeed. First, it defines how and when you have access to your monster &quot;magic&quot;, the powers that aren't common of just existing as that kind of creature. Second, they are the Rolling Trait for such powers. All rolls to use this &quot;magic&quot; substitutes Equip bonus for this Rolling Trait. And one of the things to both differentiate characters inside a splat and balance splats is to have a variety in this SSA. So you can't start being good at every magic, and it costs a lot to just trying that.<br /> <br /> You break that core principle if you make all Renown into just one. It seems feesible when you compare to the Renown system of Apocalypse, but in truth is more similar to Requiem Disciplines or Awakening Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T15:07:16-07:00","id":594178,"title":"","content":"The Breaking point examples list isn't comprehensive, you're encouraged to make your own. I mean, if you not only killed someone, but you did it to wear their skin like a suit, that's at least a -2 to the spirit breaking point, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T20:01:45-07:00","id":594361,"title":"","content":"Good points, thanks!<br /> <br /> Monte: I'm not deeply familiar with Vampire, and we're only pulling a very little from WtF2 so far, with our core system still being *mostly* WtF1-driven. I'm not sure where Renown becomes an interesting stat on par with Arcana (which I'm a little more familiar with). I can't get past the idea that Renown is a speedbump stat. &quot;Can you impress some spirit enough to impart a bit of it's power?&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Well, why can't we use Social to convince it to?&quot; &quot;Aren't we supposed to roleplay impressing people and entities, or bargain with them?&quot; &quot;If Fera need this Respect or Renown stuff to get by, why don't Magi or Vampires or plain old humans?&quot; &quot;Isn't being famous just a Merit?&quot; &quot;I don't want to be famous if we're supposed to be hiding in the shadows all the time!&quot; .... all those would be the sort of answers I'd get back. <br /> <br /> Actually, before we started talking about this system, I got so much ambivalence about Renown that I had to remind my players to mark down dots. <br /> <br /> If I'm following your line of reasoning, Renowns are separated from Respects specifically because nWoD Changing Breeds is not meant to interact with Spirits the same way that cWoD Changing Breeds was meant to? And that the Uratha are intended to have five &quot;Arcana-like&quot; measurements of their progress?<br /> <br /> How do you present Renown to reinforce the idea that Renown is a level of achievement, rather than an XP sink?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Both: As for breaking points, we haven't examined that concept yet. We have forward momentum as a first-ed centric game, so we're mining WtF2 for ideas and fixes in between story arcs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (for what it's worth, the WtF2 Grapple rules have changed Grappling from an occasional annoyance to a primary combat tactic, so many banana stickers to award for that!)<br /> <br /> If I'm following the idea, breaking points are similar to the list of sins from first ed? <br /> <br /> With that in mind, I'm getting a bit of an idea here: What if raising Harmony of Spirit or Harmony of Flesh into four or five dots comes with one of the specializations mentioned plus a breaking point.... and what if dropping to one comes with a Derangement? <br /> <br /> I'll review that section of WtF2 asap and see if we're onto something here!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, thanks to both! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T22:45:57-07:00","id":594458,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Breaking Points are the new name for sins. Its to make it more neutral. The core idea is that the things that incur a Breaking Point aren't because you &quot;did wrong&quot;, but because they tax your mental integrity, they traumatize you on some level. In WoD Core 2ed, by the way, Morality was changed to Integrity, and a lot of rules change.<br /> <br /> Is an interesting change, specialy for humans. For Werewolfs I think the change could be better, but is already better than 1ed Harmony (its still Harmony, though).<br /> <br /> And yes, I know the list isn't exaustive. I still think it could be better.<br /> <br /> Well, the thing about Renown is the distinction between its description and its mechanical function. If you read the rules on both editions, you'll see there are no rule to deal socialy with spirits using Renown. What passes for that is just the rule for Rank. But them, go read the books about spirits, specialy the &quot;blue&quot; Book of Spirits, and you'll see something very, very important: Rank isn't social status, in any way, among spirits. Its a metter of strength. A spirit knows instinctively if another is of equal, higher or lower Rank, and that says to it the comparative power of the other and that's all.<br /> <br /> So, Rank is a show of strength. An Uratha with higher Rank isn't by himself more or less than other on anyone's eyes. The books will promptly say that each Pack deals with social organization as they see fit. A Rank 5 werewolf will probably be known ina wide area and respected, but because of the things he did to be Rank 5, not because of the Rank per se. What it WILL do for you is that a Rank 4 spirit instinctively recognize a Rank 4 Uratha as an equal in power. He will be cautious, because the Uratha can defeat him in battle with some effort.<br /> <br /> That said, on both editions Renown have precisely the same function, even with the gifts themselves changing a lot:<br /> <br /> 1- You need Renown at X level to buy an X level Gift. As you need Discipline in X level to access its X level power, or Arcana X level to access its X level rotes.<br /> <br /> 2- When you use the Gift, you roll Attribute + Hability + Renown, as a Vampire uses Attribute + Hability + Discipline and Mage uses Attribute + Hability + Arcana.<br /> <br /> 3- To raise your mojo, you pays X to raise Renown. It instantly gives you a new Gift. Well, not only it work the same way in Vamp and Mage, go look in the books: they cost the same!<br /> <br /> Can you see it working? No matter how its described, it does have a clear function: to set your way to do your custom magic, the one that set you apart from other of you own splat. You'll will allways have a set of Names that are Ranked to give you Dice &amp; set your Power Level. You'll fill the rest of the dice pool with Attribute + Hability. Sometimes you'll use Power Trait instead, as Changelings use Wyrd + Contract and Mages use Gnosis + Arcana, but the basic rules are the same.<br /> <br /> No, nWoD Changing Breeds wheren't meant to interact with spirits that way. It wasn't at any time the intent of them. Instead, we have a function (why they did them, for what) and a reasoning (how they explain it on the setting). The nWoD CB function is for you to have a plethora of options to CREATE unique characters and creatures based on the idea of a born shapechanger. So they can have access to spirit magic, but you could also avoid completely dealing with spirits and make a lineage of sorcerous werecats with Mage-like rotes, or you could avoid both and make a werewolf with feral capabilities and nothing to do whatsoever with any kind of magic. You do what you want to do. The nWoD CB reasoning is that sometimes people are born with a kind of Animal-Soul not really linked to the Shadow, but only to his soul indeed, and this gives him a kind of link with that animal species and the power to shapechange. In that way, the CBs are more feral, actualy, than the Uratha, because they are something of the Material animal world, whyle Uratha are spirit-beings, lnked to spirit-wolfs, not to real wolfs. They are similar, but the difference is relevant.<br /> <br /> For sure, the Uratha mechanicaly have five Arcana-like measurements of &quot;magical&quot; progress. It already does make it easier for them compared with another splats. By myself, I like to reason them not as fame between spirits or other creatures, but toward Luna itself. Mother Luna see her children and grant them the power of Gifts, for spirits are entitled with the hability to awake this power, but not to perform it. So Luna have to see your value to make the Renown possible as a spiritual mark in your ephemera, even if is a spirit who awake the power of the Gift, or another Uratha whom perform the rite to reveal the mark Luna put upon you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T22:46:37-07:00","id":594459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=594361#post594361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points, thanks!<br /> <br /> Monte: I'm not deeply familiar with Vampire, and we're only pulling a very little from WtF2 so far, with our core system still being *mostly* WtF1-driven. I'm not sure where Renown becomes an interesting stat on par with Arcana (which I'm a little more familiar with). I can't get past the idea that Renown is a speedbump stat. &amp;quot;Can you impress some spirit enough to impart a bit of it's power?&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Well, why can't we use Social to convince it to?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Aren't we supposed to roleplay impressing people and entities, or bargain with them?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;If Fera need this Respect or Renown stuff to get by, why don't Magi or Vampires or plain old humans?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Isn't being famous just a Merit?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;I don't want to be famous if we're supposed to be hiding in the shadows all the time!&amp;quot; .... all those would be the sort of answers I'd get back.<br /> <br /> Actually, before we started talking about this system, I got so much ambivalence about Renown that I had to remind my players to mark down dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please understand, I mean no offense by this, but if these are the kinds of questions your players are asking about Renown, the only answer you can really give is &quot;read the book,&quot; because it sounds like they lack even a basic understanding of what Renown <i>is</i> and what it means within the context of the story. I'm not surprised they were so disinterested that they forgot to track it on their character sheets - it's pretty hard to care about some dots on the sheet when you don't understand what they represent in-game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=594361#post594361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm following your line of reasoning, Renowns are separated from Respects specifically because nWoD Changing Breeds is not meant to interact with Spirits the same way that cWoD Changing Breeds was meant to? And that the Uratha are intended to have five &amp;quot;Arcana-like&amp;quot; measurements of their progress?<br /> <br /> How do you present Renown to reinforce the idea that Renown is a level of achievement, rather than an XP sink?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, Renown was kind of an XP sink - it served a purpose in the narrative, but it did cost a lot of XP for what amounted to a speed bump to the best powers. In 2e, Renown is much more like Arcana (though the analogy is pretty shaky. I would highly recommend giving 2e a thorough read because the Renown and Gifts system is much more elegant and streamlined than it was in 1e. But in a nutshell, each Gift (in 1e parlance, Gift List) has five Facets, one associated with each Renown. As your Renown increases, any Facets you know that are associated with that Renown become more powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=594361#post594361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both: As for breaking points, we haven't examined that concept yet. We have forward momentum as a first-ed centric game, so we're mining WtF2 for ideas and fixes in between story arcs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (for what it's worth, the WtF2 Grapple rules have changed Grappling from an occasional annoyance to a primary combat tactic, so many banana stickers to award for that!)<br /> <br /> If I'm following the idea, breaking points are similar to the list of sins from first ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're literally just a different name for the same thing. The only real difference is the presentation. Instead of being punished for violating a moral code, you're becoming more or less spirit-like as a result of your spirit-like or human-like behavior. No moral judgment associated with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:06:01-07:00","id":594819,"title":"","content":"I still sustain: Renown are EXACTLY like Arcana. No less, no more, and precisely the same thing on both editions.<br /> <br /> What did changed, and it is a lot of difference indeed, is the associated magical systems. For sure Gifts work very distinctly from other splats' powers, specially on 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> But the core function of Renown itself is the same. Even in 1st ed it being kind of a speedbump to get higher level Gifts, since you could get them by investing in just one Renown, you still had to buy the others for the increase in the Gifts' Dice Pools.<br /> <br /> Now in 2nd ed you have even more reason to buy other Renown instead of just increase one like crazy, but the core workings of the Renown is still the same, and the same of the Arcana-Like traits on other lines. What differ isn't those traits, but the associated &quot;magic&quot; system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T12:27:30-07:00","id":594916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=594819#post594819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still sustain: Renown are EXACTLY like Arcana. No less, no more, and precisely the same thing on both editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean it's exactly like the thing - except for all the ways it isn't exactly like the thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T13:57:54-07:00","id":594998,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's both mechanically different and conceptually different. There are definite similarities, but they're by no means exactly alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:06:33-07:00","id":595004,"title":"","content":"Dunno. I don't get a fifth of all the Cunning Gifts when I take a dot there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T15:56:21-07:00","id":595074,"title":"","content":"Well, I already explained why they're the same. Each and every line uses the same system for those traits.<br /> <br /> The system for &quot;magic&quot; isn't the same, obviously. Disciplines don't work entirely like Gifts or Spells. But the &quot;Magic Trait&quot; that back-up those powers is just an aspect of the whole system, and this crucial aspect is the very same.<br /> <br /> You have a collection of traits that give dice to some powers, cost the same in all gamelines and give you access to power level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T10:16:43-07:00","id":597054,"title":"","content":"I'll put the Renown clarification to my group and we'll decide what we want to do with it. Thanks, again, for all the comments! <br /> <br /> I also have a to-do to re-examine breaking points as a clarification or replacement for the list o'sins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:58:33-07:00","id":597124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=595074#post595074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I already explained why they're the same. Each and every line uses the same system for those traits.<br /> <br /> The system for &quot;magic&quot; isn't the same, obviously. Disciplines don't work entirely like Gifts or Spells. But the &quot;Magic Trait&quot; that back-up those powers is just an aspect of the whole system, and this crucial aspect is the very same.<br /> <br /> You have a collection of traits that give dice to some powers, cost the same in all gamelines and give you access to power level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an artifact of how the system as a whole works.<br /> <br /> And they really <i>don't</i> all cost the same - Renown is 3xp per, Disciplines are 4xp per (with a 1xp cost break if they're favored), I'm not sure about how much Mage's stuff is going to cost, and Changeling/Demon/Beast don't <i>have</i> a scaling one-to-five scale. If you go by &quot;have the same cost throughout gamelines&quot;, &quot;give dice to some powers&quot;, and give you access to stuff, <i>Integrity equivalents</i> are an Arcana.<br /> <br /> It's all an artifact of how, in 2e, there are exactly 5 different prices you can put on something (nothing costs 6xp, and nothing costs less than 1xp without coming free with your template) - it's not exactly like having similar pricing <i>means</i> anything in such a case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:28:38-07:00","id":597378,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, first, that my examination comes first from 1st ed. In 2nd ed I know they changed more things, including in this case the cost of such traits. But as far as I could see, and it was Requiem and Forsaken, the price of them was the only thing that changed in regard to these traits.<br /> <br /> And I KNOW its an arifact of how the system works. That's my whole point, in fact. Just that by reducing it to only one Renown you have an impact on a relevant system artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:42:25-07:00","id":597411,"title":"","content":"At that point you might as well just use Primal Urge. I mean, part of the reason that there are separate Renowns is to stop you from just pumping one trait high and then using it to power everything.<br /> <br /> Plus, what are you going to do with character creation? Are you going to make all Werewolves start of with Renown 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T23:35:08-07:00","id":597961,"title":"","content":"I didn't understood your point. Was it to me or to the OP? I'm talking about that precisely because I think Renown should remain at 5, in the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T01:08:54-07:00","id":598045,"title":"","content":"I'd be down with treating your renown as influences if I could wrap my head around what Influence (Purity) \u2022\u2022\u2022 would even <i>mean</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:53:33-07:00","id":598458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=598045#post598045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be down with treating your renown as influences if I could wrap my head around what Influence (Purity) \u2022\u2022\u2022 would even <i>mean</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be able to strengthen, manipulate, or control Purity. Make someone or something more or less pure, change the nature of their purity, etc. Could be useful for curing poison or disease, cleaning food or water supplies, enhancing the quality of minerals, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:54:43-07:00","id":598590,"title":"","content":"No, if he's talking about the Renown, it would be more a kind of Moral Purity. Maybe you could cleanse someone's mind of interfering thought patterns with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T19:58:00-07:00","id":598954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=598590#post598590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, if he's talking about the Renown, it would be more a kind of Moral Purity. Maybe you could cleanse someone's mind of interfering thought patterns with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow both. Of course, I tend towards very broad interpretations when it comes to Influences (apparently). For example, I allow Influence in water to affect water vapor and water ice, which it seems a lot of people disagree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:22:27-07:00","id":599429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=597411#post597411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At that point you might as well just use Primal Urge. I mean, part of the reason that there are separate Renowns is to stop you from just pumping one trait high and then using it to power everything.<br /> <br /> Plus, what are you going to do with character creation? Are you going to make all Werewolves start of with Renown 2?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact, yes. Our entire pack had a couple Renowns of 1, with one at 2. Since then it's gone up fairly uniformly to 2's and edging toward a 3 for each. A very astute question, actually, because talking about everybody having the &quot;about the same but a little better at X Renown&quot; is what sparked the initial idea here!<br /> <br /> We'd been handling the need to specialize a character by using the favored / unfavored XP costs for Gifts to channel them toward their themes.<br /> <br /> Also, we have a house guideline that we use. At character creation, 4-dot anything is character-defining and you only get one, if at all. 5-dot anything is chronicle-defining and you only get that if the whole party wants to play a game significantly centered around that thing. As the chronicle progresses the bars get raised, of course. They can also be adjusted up or down to fit the themes: Scion or Exalted would have a high bar. Mortals would be lower. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:32:21-07:00","id":599440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=598045#post598045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be down with treating your renown as influences if I could wrap my head around what Influence (Purity) \u2022\u2022\u2022 would even <i>mean</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting Renown as Influence is .... BRILLIANT! That actually explains the intent much more clearly. <br /> <br /> Influences/Renowns often overlap already anyway, as Monteparnas and Charlaquin both observed. Purity and Wrath would be two good examples - both are the <i>rawr-smash</i> warriors' Renowns from their respective sources, but they aren't entirely the same. I'd allow many of the same Gifts, but Purity would not get you Gifts for despicable battle tactics and Wrath would not get you Gifts for minimizing collateral damage. <br /> <br /> +1XP all around the table.... I think we've struck gold!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T17:52:19-07:00","id":600014,"title":"","content":"Agreed!<br /> <br /> Tough mechanicaly it could still work the same way, it would be a lot more interesting for Forsaken and for your CBs to use in-setting Influences instead of Renown. And even keeping just five, we could change some of them for more relevant names. Maybe tweak the Gifts to better fit this concept, but it isn't really necessary yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T18:25:49-07:00","id":600059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=600014#post600014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed!<br /> <br /> Tough mechanicaly it could still work the same way, it would be a lot more interesting for Forsaken and for your CBs to use in-setting Influences instead of Renown. And even keeping just five, we could change some of them for more relevant names. Maybe tweak the Gifts to better fit this concept, but it isn't really necessary yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been bouncing around so many possibilities in my head, it's been tempting to get the white-out and improve my WtF1 and WtF2 books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Because Influence is also exactly proportional to Rank, just like (the stat formerly known as) Renown being proportional to Rank, this lets us describe our furry heroes as anything from being wise, to mighty, to socially-among-spirits-influential. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T11:30:28-07:00","id":600792,"title":"","content":"With Influence we could, also, give a more mystical bent to the stats, tough such would require some thinkering with Gifts.<br /> <br /> Just as a quick tough exercise we could have: Body, Mind, Spirit, Animals and Elements.<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if we just keep to the default, but thinking it as Influence instead of Renown, it makes WAY more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T16:16:27-07:00","id":601030,"title":"","content":"Here's a test second-rewrite/clarification of Renown into Influence. What do you guys think? (Keep in mind, I'm running a mixed breeds game, not strictly Forsaken, though our pack's favorite allies are Forsaken)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (beta rewrite 2)<br /> <br /> Renown (and Respect) is replaced by Influence.<br /> <br /> As a Therian progresses in power and understanding, their Influence with the matters of spirit increase. <br /> <br /> This acts much like a Spirit's Influence, in that it represents a measure of power. It does not grant the same arbitrary command over the Influenced subject that a Spirit enjoys, but it does both enable and empower a Therian's Gifts. <br /> <br /> The five Renowns and five Respects are available as Influences. Like Spirit Influences, others may be defined, with similar guidelines. Not all Therians must have the core five or five.<br /> <br /> Influence is displayed as tattooing or branding on the skin. Children of Luna are often marked with silver tattoos which glow in the Umbra. Other traditions may use other options. <br /> <br /> Influence also has a social aspect, much like the Renown rules. Spirits and other Spirit-tied characters (including Therians) often compare Influence to determine their relative rank. Influence as a measure of reputation often precedes a character - Spirits whisper and any Therian can readily see silver tattoos in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Lunar silver tattoos (and those of some other traditions) may be empowered by 1 Essence to glow brightly for a Scene. This is bright enough to be faintly visible in the material world. Doing so among the Forsaken is considered a sign of respect, though it inspires much chest-thumping and trash talking. Doing so among other species has varying interpretations.<br /> <br /> To gain a Gift, the Therian must have sufficient Influence to obtain it. The linked Influence should be the same as listed, or a sensible alternative. Notice that similar Influences may not include all of the same thing. Purity would not include Gifts for despicable combat tactics, nor Wrath include Gifts for limiting collateral damage, even though both of them are suitable Influences for the gifts of warriors.<br /> <br /> When a Gift is obtained, it is forever tied to the particular Influence that enabled it. (extra-special beta-test rule follows) In all cases, any roll to use the Gift includes that Influence in the dice pool.<br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T03:03:55-07:00","id":601550,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty good to me. I would use that. In fact, I WILL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T18:15:55-07:00","id":602399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=601550#post601550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty good to me. I would use that. In fact, I WILL.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *bro-paw*<br /> <br /> I'm going to put this to my players tonight on our Obsidian Portal site and dig in to it properly with our next game session. <br /> <br /> Please let me know if you find any breaks or opportunities! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T21:40:45-07:00","id":626299,"title":"","content":"So far we're having pretty good success!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T01:55:12-07:00","id":626434,"title":"","content":"Good to know.<br /> <br /> My players have being more interested in Vampire for now, cWoD Mage and crossovers, and Monster Hearts. We aren't going to play Forsaken for a while, so I hadn't the chance to try Renown as Influence yet.<br /> <br /> How are the play-tests going?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:02:16-07:00","id":626776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=626434#post626434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the play-tests going?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the pro side, the new explanation for Influences makes a lot more sense and really turned the light on for my players. We started going through our Gifts and figuring out which will be having the bonuses from Influence ratings.<br /> <br /> A couple of questions we're working through: Since we're using Changing Breeds (closer to the cWoD sense of Garou-peers than the nWoD sense of manimals) we had a question whether they apply to Aspects and things as well. For the moment we're going with yes, with an explanation that the Nauhaul (beast-spirit) brings along its own Gifts, simply with an intrinsic rather than extrinsic source. <br /> <br /> Also, a lot of our Gifts have a static dice modifier rather than a dice pool. For now, we're going with the Influence *not* modifying those. A fair number of them would quickly be doubled or more by adding Influence to the static modifier. I'd like to add a bonus for those, but we haven't figured out a way yet. <br /> <br /> On the con side, it's a rules change in an ongoing Chronicle, so there's inevitably going to be some mismatches to figure out. We have a few characters who will need to re-shop for a Gift or two, and everybody's rethinking their plans for Influence.<br /> <br /> The perks for Harmony of Flesh and Harmony of Spirit have been very popular. It's a little work up front to explain how the perks work, but it seems to be a good way for characters to be distinctive. We're still working through how we want to do sins / breaking points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:40:52-07:00","id":626936,"title":"","content":"What kind of Gifts you keep with static dice pools? And why for now?<br /> <br /> I can't think easily of Breaking Points for Harmony, but the devs couldn't really think of them, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:34:53-07:00","id":626982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/593798-variations-on-renown-and-harmony-critique-and-ideas?p=626936#post626936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of Gifts you keep with static dice pools? And why for now?<br /> <br /> I can't think easily of Breaking Points for Harmony, but the devs couldn't really think of them, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>For example &quot;The Right Word&quot; adds a static +2 to all Social rolls under the right situations. Adding an Influence to that would be 50% to 250% of the bonus itself!<br /> <br /> As for Breaking Points, so far the thinking is to take &quot;a bit&quot; from the existing Harmony list and &quot;a bit&quot; from the Oaths of the Moon (depending on what critter-spirit the character has) and go from there. How many of each is up for some discussion yet. Since we're still using the Virtue and Vice system, some Breaking Points risk redundancy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't eat people&quot; is pretty easy, and I think would be common, with the understanding that (in our Chronicle) the Pure specifically don't have that Breaking Point. <br /> <br /> We already had a wonderful scene in-game that differentiated &quot;Don't kill&quot; from &quot;Don't murder&quot;, and had a Morality roll backing it up. We don't play scenes like this very often, but it was quite meaningful to our story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:19:35-07:00","id":627043,"title":"","content":"Ok, Influence should indeed be added mostly to rolls to activate the Gift, when needed. Tough I'm not sure if adding Influence as bonus is such a bad thing. Overall, Influence should have an impact on the mystical prowess, so it does make sense to add it.<br /> <br /> You could mostly make the Oaths of the given Fera into Breaking Points for Spirit and take some key sins of old Morality as Breaking Points for Flesh. Or, better yet, take the new Breaking Points of 2nd ed Humanity as basis for Flesh. Given your focus, I think it would work well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}